<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01UK">Proposition <span data-tag="01UK">5.1.4.13</span>.</a> Let $q: X \rightarrow S$ be a cartesian fibration of simplicial sets and let $\sigma : \Delta ^2 \rightarrow X$ be a $2$-simplex of $X$, which we will depict as a diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  y \ar [dr]^{g} &amp;  \\ x \ar [ur]^{f} \ar [rr]^-{h} &amp;  &amp;  z. } \]
</div>
<p> Suppose that $g$ is $q$-cartesian. Then $f$ is $q$-cartesian if and only if $h$ is $q$-cartesian. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Proposition <a data-tag="01U4" href="/tag/01U4">5.1.3.7</a> with Remark <a data-tag="01UE" href="/tag/01UE">5.1.4.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
